# Build-context ignore for DotSoundBackend/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit (default in Docker Compose v2) reads "<dockerfile>.dockerignore"
# next to the Dockerfile, so this file governs the parent build context
# (..) that holds both DotSoundBackend and the sibling private core.
# Patterns are relative to that context root. Its job: keep secrets, VCS
# metadata, local databases, and caches out of every image layer — most
# importantly the private core's local .env must never bake into an image.

# Secrets / local environment
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
**/secrets.json
**/credentials.json
**/service-account*.json

# VCS metadata and local history-rewrite backups
**/.git
**/.git-coauthor-backups
**/.git-history-backups
**/.git-release-backups

# Local databases / dumps
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db

# Python / tooling caches and artifacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov

# Local virtualenv and frontend deps (the image installs its own)
**/.venv
**/node_modules
